    Fix capture agents in other organizations never being marked offline (#8271)
    
    Fixes #7885.
    
    The agent cache's RemovalListener, which marks an expired agent offline,
    used securityService.getOrganization() - the organization of whichever
    thread happened to trigger the eviction - instead of the organization
    already encoded in the cache key (agentName;==;org). In a multi-tenant
    deployment, eviction processed on behalf of one organization could not
    find another organization's agent, the resulting NotFoundException was
    swallowed, and that agent was never transitioned to offline.
    
    Split the org out of the key the same way the cache loader already does,
    instead of asking securityService for the calling thread's organization.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Proper testing requires a multi-tenant setup, but testing the included
    test might be good enough?
    
